WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.893
(upbeat music)

2
00:00:02.893 --> 00:00:06.430
Food, I love eating it, talking about it,

3
00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.033
watching it on TV.

4
00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.839
Here is some delicious kitchen inspiration.

5
00:00:10.839 --> 00:00:11.672
(air whooshing)

6
00:00:11.672 --> 00:00:12.505
Hi, Drew.

7
00:00:12.505 --> 00:00:14.630 line:15%
I'm Jessie, founder of Life As A Strawberry.

8
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:15.780 line:15%
And today I'm teaching you

9
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.060 line:15%
how to make my favorite simple cranberry sauce

10
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.450
for the holidays.

11
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.390
Start by adding 12 ounces of cranberries

12
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.600
to a small sauce pan with a bit of maple syrup and honey,

13
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.480
this is gonna help us balance out the tartness

14
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.870
of these cranberries.

15
00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.800
Add a splash of water and the juice of one orange slice,

16
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.620
then tuck that orange right into the pot

17
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.330
along with everything else.

18
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.640
Add a pinch of salt and 1/2 of a cinnamon stick

19
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.270
for some great depth of flavor,

20
00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.770
then stir it all up and cook over low heat

21
00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.550
for 15 to 20 minutes, just until the cranberries

22
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.830
start to burst and break down.

23
00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:48.950
Remove the orange slice and the cinnamon stick from the pot.

24
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.400
And if you don't love this chunky cranberry sauce,

25
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.790
you can use an immersion blender

26
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.710
to smooth it all out a little bit before you serve.

27
00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.810
This is a great make-ahead recipe.

28
00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.720
You can serve it immediately or let it cool

29
00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.620
and stored in the fridge for up to a week

30
00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.550
or the freezer for several months.

31
00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:04.710
When you're ready to eat,

32
00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.355
top with a bit of fresh orange zest and enjoy.

33
00:01:07.355 --> 00:01:08.470
(air whooshing)

34
00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:12.048
That recipe looks muah!
(lips smacking)

35
00:01:12.048 --> 00:01:14.631
(upbeat music)

